WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.680
Aging -- that's the subject of my
upcoming book, "How Not to Age."

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:09.800
This video will give you just a
taste of the body of evidence

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:13.334
I'll be covering in the book.
Check it out.

00:00:13.334 --> 00:00:19.979
"The Best Diet for Healthy Aging"

00:00:21.652 --> 00:00:25.360
Based on a study of more
than 400,000 people,

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:30.000
replacing just 3% of calories of
animal protein with plant protein

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.040
was associated with a 10%
reduction in overall mortality risk.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:38.280
That comes out to be
about an extra year of life,

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:42.400
swapping out just 3% of any
animal protein with plant protein.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:46.840
And egg protein was the worst,
mostly found in the egg whites.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:50.840
Swapping 3% of calories of
egg protein for plant protein

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:54.960
was associated with more than
a 20% reduction in overall mortality,

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:56.280
worse than red meat.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:01.160
But it's not just about adding years
to your life, but life to your years.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:05.040
What about changes in dietary intake
of animal versus vegetable protein

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:09.600
and unhealthy aging?
Healthy aging is defined as

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.400
"the process of developing
and maintaining

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:16.440
the functional ability that
enables wellbeing in older age."

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:20.640
No one wants to just be a vegetable,
and you may be able to avoid that

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.120
by eating more vegetables.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:25.520
A higher intake of vegetable
protein was associated with

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:28.920
less accumulation of deficits,
based on functional impairments,

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:32.920
self-reported health and vitality,
mental health and diseases,

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:35.480
and the use of health services.

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:38.880
Swapping in just 1% of vegetable
protein calories for animal protein

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:43.040
led to significantly less
deficit accumulation.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:46.800
Now you may be thinking, duh,
animal protein and animal fat

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:48.880
travel alongside each
other in the same foods,

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:52.520
so maybe this is all just a
saturated fat effect. But no,

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:55.360
even after accounting for fat,
there still seemed to be something

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:58.480
about the animal versus
plant protein sources,

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:01.200
though it's still not clear if
the beneficial health effects

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:04.440
are because of the avoidance
of deleterious effects associated

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:07.560
with animal foods or the
beneficial effects of plants,

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.400
though it may be a bit of both.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:13.440
A recent review in a
dermatology journal on the role

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:15.680
of a whole-food, plant-based
diet in preventing

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:19.640
and reversing skin aging
emphasized this point.

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:24.720
A whole-food, plant-based diet is not
the same thing as just a vegan diet.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:28.280
You can have a terribly
unhealthy vegan diet.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:32.280
As a physician, "vegan" just
tells me what you don't eat,

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:36.760
but you actually have to like
to eat your vegetables, too.

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:38.720
But when you do,
a whole-food, plant-based diet

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.720
can aid in the prevention,
and in some cases reversal,

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:45.040
of some of the leading chronic
diseases in the United States

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:48.200
as well as the potential for
younger-looking skin due to

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.520
telomere lengthening,

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:52.120
maximizing the antioxidant
potential of our cells,

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:55.600
and also eliminating harmful
carcinogens and aging toxins,

00:02:55.600 --> 00:03:00.040
known as gerontotoxins,
from entering our bloodstream.

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:03.640
No wonder the highest life
expectancy of any formally

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:06.160
described population
in the world may be

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:09.520
the Adventist vegetarians
in Loma Linda, California,

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:12.440
one of the five original
"blue zones" in the world.

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:15.600
The average life expectancy of
Adventist vegetarian men and women

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:19.240
is into their 80's, about
6 to 10 years longer

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:23.160
than the general population
in California, with vegetarian,

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:26.560
exercising, nut eating, lower
weight, never smokers living

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:29.680
about 9 to 11 years longer than
those lacking those qualities.

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:35.120
So that's like 10 years of life
up for grabs.

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:38.720
Now, substantial gains in life
expectancy would only be worthwhile

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:42.840
if they were also accompanied by
a longer period of good quality life.

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:46.040
Although overall well-being
has not been measured directly,

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:49.560
vegetarian Adventists have been
recorded taking fewer medications,

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:52.920
and logging fewer overnight hospital
stays and surgical procedures

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:54.600
and x-ray examinations,

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:57.920
and the reduced prevalence of
several chronic diseases alone

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:02.440
would presumably make
life likely more worth living.

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:04.720
The most feared disease
associated with getting older

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:06.960
is likely Alzheimer's disease.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:10.280
Dementia is one of our fastest
growing epidemics, affecting

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:13.760
1 in 10 individuals older
than 65 years of age

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:18.520
and half of all individuals
older than 85.

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:22.240
Alzheimer's is the main type,
and indeed the most feared.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:25.880
So when we're talking about
"Plant-Based Diets for Healthy Aging,"

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:28.840
particularly intriguing is emerging
evidence that diet plays

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:32.360
a major role in the prevention
of age-related cognitive decline

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:34.200
and Alzheimer's disease.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:38.000
It has been shown that a diet
rich in fruits, grains, beans,

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.640
vegetables, nuts, and seeds
may cut the risk of Alzheimer's

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:44.320
disease by more than a half.

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:46.040
This is the study
they're talking about,

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:50.200
the so-called MIND diet, which
emphasizes natural plant foods,

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:52.560
including specifically berries,
the healthiest fruits,

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:54.800
and greens,
the healthiest vegetables,

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:58.280
while limiting the intakes of animal
and high saturated fat foods

00:04:58.280 --> 00:04:59.560
like meat and dairy.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:04.560
Stricter adherence to the MIND diet
was associated with a 53% reduction

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:06.440
in risk for Alzheimer's disease.

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:10.600
In fact, even moderate adherence
appeared to cut risk by a third.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:13.440
Overall, participants who showed
high adherence to the diet

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:19.160
had cognitive functioning equivalent
to a person who was 7.5 years younger.

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:22.080
No wonder people who ate meat,
including poultry and fish,

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:24.720
were more than twice as
likely to become demented

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:27.760
as their vegetarian counterparts,
and we're talking three times

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:31.320
the risk when past meat consumption
was taken into account.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:34.680
This may be because plant-based
diets are known to preserve

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:37.600
body tissues from both
oxidative stress and inflammation,

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:41.480
hallmarks of these kinds
of degenerative diseases.

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:43.680
That may be why
berries are so protective,

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:45.800
since they're so rich in antioxidants,

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:48.520
and in terms of inflammation
those who avoid meat display

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:51.320
a higher abundance of
anti-inflammatory compounds

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:52.880
flowing through their systems

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:57.800
and lower levels of pro-inflammatory
indicators like C-reactive protein.

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:02.040
Dietary factors also influence the
effect of stress on cognitive decline.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:05.440
Diets characterized by high intake
of animal proteins, saturated fats,

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:09.280
and added sugars, along with
low intakes of plant-based foods,

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:12.000
can increase secretion
of corticosteroids,

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.640
stress hormones like cortisol
from the adrenal glands,

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:18.560
which may promote the development
of Alzheimer's disease.

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:22.600
Then there are the gerontotoxins,
the aging toxins like AGEs,

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:24.520
advanced glycation end-products,

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:28.360
in our diet that may be a factor in
the development of Alzheimer's.

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:32.560
Safe foods, foods that contain
low AGE content, include starches

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:35.160
like whole grains, beans,
fruits, and vegetables,

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:38.080
whereas the worst sources
in the diet are broiled,

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:42.560
grilled, fried, or roasted meats.
The cooking process is important.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:46.840
Chicken breast has an AGE content
of 1,000 units when boiled in water,

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:48.440
like chicken soup or something,

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:52.400
but that same chicken breast
jumps up to 9,000 when broiled.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:57.000
Here s a list of the top 40
most AGE-contaminated foods

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:03.160
tested in terms of AGEs per serving.
As you can see it's almost all meat:

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:07.000
chicken, bacon, hot dogs,
and on down the list.

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:10.240
I tell people to choose raw
nuts and seeds to avoid AGEs,

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:15.960
but even roasted, toasted nuts
don't come close to making the list.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:17.560
Now, of course, it's not just diet.

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:20.400
We need to get adequate sleep,
rest, and physical activity.

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:24.720
For example, daily brisk walks were
associated with a 40% lower risk

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:26.760
of developing Alzheimer's later in life,

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:31.080
and smoking may double your
risk of developing dementia.

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:33.680
But in terms of preventing
Alzheimer's with diet,

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:36.000
the key takeaways
are the following:

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:38.720
reduce added sugars,
saturated fat, animal products,

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:40.360
and processed foods in general,

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:44.440
while eating more plants,
especially greens and beans,

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:47.993
fruit, especially berries,
and reduce added salt.

